From 48e6b709d8f8639e4ba575661d66040961c6b44b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:05:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 248/248] fix(kanban): a recovered quota wall never becomes a
 human block [daveey]

Problem: six cards sat blocked kind=capability for ~13 h (2026-10-23) with
"Held in ready by the respawn guard (blocker_auth) ... Last error: pid N exited
rate-limited (quota wall)" after the wall had cleared.
Why: the rate-limit requeue stamps last_failure_error; a later non-failure run
(changes_requested/blocked) became the latest run, so the outcome=rate_limited
cooldown branch no longer fired and the stamp matched _RESPAWN_BLOCKER_RE as
blocker_auth; the 30-min hold cap then blocked it as capability (a human kind).

- Quota/rate-limit/429 text (no auth signal) takes the rate_limit_cooldown path
  whatever the latest outcome; once the cooldown elapses the stamp is cleared
  (also on the rate_limited-outcome path) and the card retries.
- Hold cap on a quota-flavored error or rate_limit_cooldown re-queues (clears
  the stamp) instead of blocking. Real auth errors still block capability.
- Dispatcher tick releases existing guard-hold capability/needs_input blocks on
  a quota error once another card completed after the block, with a comment.
